BusyBox in term51
=================

The file busybox in this folder of the package is BusyBox 1.38.0 for
BlackBerry 10, exactly as released by

    https://github.com/XIAZY/busybox-qnx

under the tag named in term51's tools/busybox.lock (v1.38.0-qnx1 at the
time of writing). term51 does not change or build it: its build downloads
the released file and checks its sha256. The source of that file, with
every change made to BusyBox for QNX and the way to build the same bytes
again, is that repository at that tag; its qnx/README.md says which tools
are in it and why some are not.

BusyBox is free software under the GNU General Public License, version 2:
see LICENSE here. Its option parsing on QNX comes from musl libc, under
the MIT licence: see musl-getopt.MIT. The program also contains helper
functions of LLVM's compiler-rt (Apache License 2.0 with LLVM exceptions)
and parts of the BlackBerry 10 SDK's static C library, which the toolchain
links in.

term51 runs it as a separate program: for the tools the phone lacks
(head, tr, id and others), found at the end of the shell's PATH, and for
the BusyBox shell (ash) that the settings offer.
